<div id="backoffice">
<p class="title">
 General settings:
</p>
Everything tCMS reads out of its configuration file lives here, grouped the way
config/default.cfg groups it.  Open the section you care about and leave the
rest folded up.
<br />
The Data Model <em>must</em> be 0-configuration.
If for example, you use mysql it will have to rely on either a local server, valid config file or connection proxy/pooler locally.
<hr />
<form class="Submissions Config" id="mainConfig" method="post" action="/config/save">
    : for $config_sections -> $section {
    <details class="config-section">
        <summary><: $section.title :></summary>
        : for $section.fields -> $field {
        <div class="config-field">
            <label for="config-<: $field.name :>"><: $field.title :></label>
            : if ( $field.comment ) {
            <p class="config-help"><: $field.comment :></p>
            : }
            : if ( $field.options ) {
            <select class="cooltext" id="config-<: $field.name :>" name="<: $field.name :>">
                : for $field.options -> $option {
                <option value="<: $option.value :>" <: if ( $option.selected ) { :>selected<: } :> ><: $option.label :></option>
                : }
            </select>
            : } else if ( $field.multiline ) {
            <textarea class="cooltext" id="config-<: $field.name :>" name="<: $field.name :>" rows="3" form="mainConfig"><: $field.value :></textarea>
            : } else {
            <input class="cooltext" type="text" id="config-<: $field.name :>" name="<: $field.name :>" value="<: $field.value :>" />
            : }
        </div>
        : }
    </details>
    : }
    <br />
    <input type="submit" class="coolbutton" value="Commit Changes" />

</form>
<hr />
<p class="title">
 Theme cloner:
</p>
Want to write your own theme?
Clone a theme here then see the <a href="https://tcms.troglodyne.net/index.php?nav=5&post=fileshare/manual/Chapter 03-Customization.post" title="GET UR MIND RITE">styling guide</a>
for information on how tCMS' templates, image sets and CSS work in the theming system.
<hr />
<form class="Submissions" id="themeCloner" method="post" action="/themeclone">
    Theme:
    <select class="cooltext" name="theme">
        : for $themes -> $theme {
        <option value="<: $theme :>"><: $theme :></option>
        : }
    </select>
    <input required type="text" class="cooltext" placeholder="newTheme" name="newtheme" />
    <input type="submit" class="coolbutton" value="Clone" />
</form>
</div>
